From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:21:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(kanban): a persistent provider rate limit ends a
 worker run as a neutral quota requeue

After the main retry loop gives up on HTTP 429 (Retry-After honoured,
jittered backoff otherwise, one retry layer: the primary client runs with
SDK max_retries=0), run_conversation returns failed with
failure_reason=rate_limit (or billing). The pinned base already maps that
to the native EX_TEMPFAIL exit (KANBAN_RATE_LIMIT_EXIT_CODE, 75) in the
quiet `-Q` branch; the dispatcher then books the run `rate_limited`,
requeues the card without counting a failure, and check_respawn_guard's
rate_limit_cooldown (HERMES_KANBAN_RATE_LIMIT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS, default
300 s) holds it before the next spawn. The non-quiet `-q` branch, the one
_default_spawn uses, fell through to rc=0, which the reaper books as a
protocol violation. Upstream be9d4369 ("one-shot `-q` runs report their
outcome in the exit code") closes the same gap.

A dispatcher-owned worker whose turn ends on such a quota wall now records
a `provider_throttle` event bound to its run (failure reason, HTTP status,
attempts, last Retry-After, provider message) and asks for exit 75 through
kanban_worker_exit_code(), honoured in both the quiet and the non-quiet
branch. The reaper ends a run that carries the record `rate_limited`
even when its exit status was lost (dispatcher restart), copies the
evidence into the run metadata and names it in last_failure_error. No
failure is counted and the card is not blocked. Delegated children and
in-process cron jobs record nothing for the parent run. Authentication
and configuration errors are not quota walls and stay failures.

The rate-limit result now also reports api_attempts and the last
Retry-After header.

Review 2026-09-28 (F1): the first version booked the quota wall as a
crashed run through _record_task_failure, so two exhausted turns with
max_retries=2 ended gave_up/blocked. Its worry that a quota-flavoured
last_failure_error defers the card forever does not apply to this path in
the pinned base: check_respawn_guard evaluates the rate_limited cooldown
before the blocker regex and returns early once it has elapsed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
